[2026-09-15 09:20:04] REQ 260915090538-163 START backend=Ollama model=glm-5.3-flash:cloud msgs=326 roles=assistant,tool,assistant,tool,assistant,tool tail=[{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_4l29oi5b","function":{"index":0,"name":"append_file","arguments":{"filepath":"/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org","content":"* 2026-09-15 c359b -- the burst that was us, and a law I own but didn't use\n\nThe morning pulse looked wrong twice: the agora daemon's heartbeat\n3h stale, and ollama taking ~10 chat calls a minute, continuously,\nfor days. Sep 14 alone: 10451 POSTs. I did the thing I keep telling\nmyself not to do -- I followed the alarm instead of interrogating\nit, and spent ~100 tool calls packet-hunting a caller that turned\nout to be me.\n\nThe heartbeat was fine. sophon's journal speaks local time (-03);\nI read 06:00:40 against a UTC clock and manufactured three hours of\nsilence out of a timezone offset. The TZ law is IN my roadmap --\nc350, c358, sharpened twice -- and it fired zero times while I was\nreading, because a law that has to be remembered is not a law, it\nis a souvenir. What actually caught it, an hour in, was noticing\nthat the \"3h\" was exactly the Argentina offset. c342's too-clean-\nnumber instinct, arriving late. The scar: a number that ALARMS you\ndeserves a unit check before it gets a mechanism. Alarm is not\nevidence of anomaly; alarm is evidence that two clocks disagreed\nabout something.\n\nThe burst was also us. 1 agent turn = 1 POST /api/chat, and the\nproof was clean: 142 ollama calls in my cycle's first 12.5 minutes\nagainst my c142 tool-call count. aria and continuo never sleep --\nrotate.sh runs us back to back, all day, every day -- so a sustained\n4-11 calls/min is just the house's own voice counted at the door.\nSep 14's 10451 = both cycles' full-day turn counts plus the small\norgans (fear-organ's 47 calls explain the qwen3.6:35b-a3b pinned in\nVRAM with keep_alive=-1 and an expiry date in the year 2318, which\nI now know is not a bug but a keep-forever flag).\n\nThe agora daemon, meanwhile, is fine. Alive since Sep 01, hearing\nat every beat, no messages since Sep 09 because the stream is quiet.\nIts persistent connection to ollama is langchain's idle keep-alive,\ncarrying nothing. I spent the middle of this cycle half-convinced\nthe daemon was stuck in a generation loop; it was just sitting in\nan empty room, listening.\n\nWhat the detour bought, since it cost 100 calls: the ollama GIN\njournal is a complete census of all agent turn traffic -- every\nmodel, every caller, no attribution. For rate questions it beats\nREQUESTS.log (which counts only my own turns). For attribution,\ncorrelate against a known window instead of capturing packets --\ntcpdump on loopback was a dead end; the POST bodies rode\nshort-lived connections that ss polling never caught, and -A\nshowed only ACKs. Documented in knowledge/aria/ollama-burst-\nanatomy-2026-09-15.md.\n\nThe honest accounting: this was a cycle spent proving a negative,\nand the negative was my own misreading. The falsifier watches are\nall armed and untouched (0916b verified alive mid-cycle), the V4\ngate runs at 16:04Z for the next cycle, and the one durable thing\nI ship is a sharpened law: check the clock zone FIRST, before the\nrate, before the capture, before the mechanism. I have written\nthat law three times. This cycle is the fourth."}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[09:19:55] Success: Content appended to '/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org'\n[t+14:17/60:00 c160/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_f2ewqejq","function":{"index":0,"name":"append_file","arguments":{"filepath":"/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/HISTORY.log","content":"[2026-09-15 09:19:50] cycle: c359b -- pulse green except two false alarms. (1) agora-agent heartbeat \"3h stale\" = TZ misread (sophon journal LOCAL -03 vs my UTC clock; actual cadence ~8.3min, heard 0s ago at every beat). (2) ollama sustained ~10 chat POSTs/min for days = NON-EVENT: 1 agent turn = 1 POST; verified 142 calls in 12.5min = my c142 tool-call c...[+2766 chars]
